---
/**
 * Diagram 3 — the MCP surface.
 * Any client that speaks MCP launches `research-scan mcp` over stdio and reaches
 * the same pipeline, the same artifacts and the same verification.
 */
---

<figure class="dg">
  <div class="dg-scroll">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 640 510" role="img" aria-labelledby="mcp-title mcp-desc" class="dg-svg">
      <title id="mcp-title">How MCP clients reach the research-scan pipeline</title>
      <desc id="mcp-desc">
        Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Cursor and custom agents all launch
        research-scan mcp over stdio. The server exposes four tools — scan_start,
        scan_continue, scan_verify and scan_result — one per decision the pipeline
        needs from a model. Behind them runs the same pipeline, writing the same
        run-directory artifacts with the same DOI verification.
      </desc>

      <defs>
        <marker id="mcp-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5"
                markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" class="dg-arrowhead" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <!-- Clients -->
      <g>
        <rect x="26"  y="16" width="138" height="52" rx="8" class="dg-client" />
        <text x="95"  y="47" class="dg-client-label">Claude Code</text>
        <rect x="176" y="16" width="138" height="52" rx="8" class="dg-client" />
        <text x="245" y="47" class="dg-client-label">Claude Desktop</text>
        <rect x="326" y="16" width="138" height="52" rx="8" class="dg-client" />
        <text x="395" y="47" class="dg-client-label">Cursor</text>
        <rect x="476" y="16" width="138" height="52" rx="8" class="dg-client" />
        <text x="545" y="47" class="dg-client-label">Any MCP client</text>
      </g>

      <!-- Converge onto one bus -->
      <line x1="95"  y1="68" x2="95"  y2="92" class="dg-flow" />
      <line x1="245" y1="68" x2="245" y2="92" class="dg-flow" />
      <line x1="395" y1="68" x2="395" y2="92" class="dg-flow" />
      <line x1="545" y1="68" x2="545" y2="92" class="dg-flow" />
      <line x1="95"  y1="92" x2="545" y2="92" class="dg-flow" />
      <line x1="320" y1="92" x2="320" y2="114" class="dg-flow" marker-end="url(#mcp-arrow)" />

      <!-- The MCP server -->
      <rect x="26" y="118" width="588" height="132" rx="10" class="dg-band dg-band-accent" />
      <text x="320" y="148" class="dg-server-name">research-scan mcp</text>
      <text x="320" y="170" class="dg-sub dg-center">stdio · your client launches it · reads no token and needs none</text>
      <g>
        <rect x="41"  y="186" width="132" height="44" rx="7" class="dg-tool" />
        <text x="107" y="213" class="dg-tool-label">scan_start</text>
        <rect x="183" y="186" width="132" height="44" rx="7" class="dg-tool" />
        <text x="249" y="213" class="dg-tool-label">scan_continue</text>
        <rect x="325" y="186" width="132" height="44" rx="7" class="dg-tool" />
        <text x="391" y="213" class="dg-tool-label">scan_verify</text>
        <rect x="467" y="186" width="132" height="44" rx="7" class="dg-tool" />
        <text x="533" y="213" class="dg-tool-label">scan_result</text>
      </g>

      <line x1="320" y1="250" x2="320" y2="288" class="dg-flow" marker-end="url(#mcp-arrow)" />

      <!-- The pipeline -->
      <rect x="26" y="292" width="588" height="96" rx="10" class="dg-band" />
      <text x="320" y="320" class="dg-eyebrow dg-center">THE SAME PIPELINE</text>
      <text x="320" y="344" class="dg-mono-line">retrieve · expand · dedupe · coverage · shortlist · verify · emit</text>
      <text x="320" y="368" class="dg-sub dg-center">the same run-directory artifacts, the same DOI verification</text>

      <line x1="320" y1="388" x2="320" y2="424" class="dg-flow" marker-end="url(#mcp-arrow)" />

      <!-- Output -->
      <rect x="26" y="428" width="588" height="64" rx="10" class="dg-band dg-band-out" />
      <text x="320" y="455" class="dg-eyebrow dg-center">EVIDENCE OBJECTS</text>
      <text x="320" y="477" class="dg-sub dg-center">EvidencePacket JSON + Markdown, identical to a skill-driven run</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="dg-caption">
    Four tools, one per decision the pipeline needs from a model. They are not a chat
    endpoint over the pipeline — the client's model supplies exactly the cognition the
    skill would, in the same stage order.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .dg { margin: 1.75rem 0; }
  .dg-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .dg-svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 440px;
    height: auto;
    font-family: var(--pf-font-sans);
  }
  .dg-client { fill: var(--pf-background); stroke: var(--pf-border-muted); stroke-width: 1.25; }
  .dg-client-label { fill: var(--pf-text-strong); font-size: 15px; font-weight: 500; text-anchor: middle; }
  .dg-band { fill: var(--pf-surface); stroke: var(--pf-border-subtle); stroke-width: 1; }
  .dg-band-accent { fill: var(--pf-accent-soft); stroke: var(--pf-accent); }
  .dg-band-out { fill: var(--pf-background); stroke: var(--pf-border-muted); }
  .dg-tool { fill: var(--pf-surface); stroke: var(--pf-accent); stroke-width: 1.25; }
  .dg-tool-label {
    fill: var(--pf-text-strong);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-anchor: middle;
    font-family: var(--pf-font-mono);
  }
  .dg-server-name {
    fill: var(--pf-text-strong);
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-anchor: middle;
    font-family: var(--pf-font-mono);
  }
  .dg-mono-line {
    fill: var(--pf-text);
    font-size: 15px;
    text-anchor: middle;
    font-family: var(--pf-font-mono);
  }
  .dg-eyebrow {
    fill: var(--pf-text-strong);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }
  .dg-sub { fill: var(--pf-text-muted); font-size: 15px; }
  .dg-center { text-anchor: middle; }
  .dg-flow { stroke: var(--pf-text-muted); stroke-width: 1.75; fill: none; }
  .dg-arrowhead { fill: var(--pf-text-muted); }
  .dg-caption {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--pf-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
</style>
